// This file is @generated by perseid, vendored from the runtime of the CLI pack.
//! `<cli> mcp --port`: the MCP server over Streamable HTTP, stateless. Each POST to `/mcp` is one
//! JSON-RPC message with its own API key, answered with JSON rather than an event stream, by a
//! clone of the server ([`Server::for_request`]): no session, no `initialize` to remember.
//! Requests of revision 2026-07-28 carry their version, client and capabilities in `_meta`, and
//! mirror the version, method and tool in `MCP-Protocol-Version`, `Mcp-Method` and `Mcp-Name`,
//! checked against the body; earlier ones name their revision in `MCP-Protocol-Version` alone.
//! Connections are served side by side on one current-thread runtime, as calls are on stdio; a
//! client that disconnects drops its call, which ends its requests.
